<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi Everyone, I have notice a machine gun like sounds from my RD-5R. I have no idea what might be wrong. Is this a hardware problem? any idea?<br><br> <strong>iframe</strong> <br><a href="http://youtu.be/gRFKIO2Zt5A">youtu.be/gRFKIO2Zt5A</a></div></blockquote>It's how DMR sounds in an analog radio, seems that your RF (DMR) is leaking into the audio. <br><br>Couldn't see how much power you use in the video but try lower power levels and a proper antenna (factory) as that stub antenna can result<br>in mismatch (high SWR) , if you have a 50 ohm dummy load it's also interesting to see if that make the interference go away.<br><br>The idea is to find out if the RF leak is internal or external.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sun Aug 25, 2024 3:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
